    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Strong cyber-editorial art direction: disciplined near-black palette, crisp cyan/red semantic accents, bold headline, and a clear desktop comparison layout. Tablet remains coherent. Mobile degrades into an exceptionally long, dense stack with very small metadata/body text, weak row scanning, and cramped two-column verdict cards. The global header also truncates the active label to “LIVE WI” on mobile, while low-contrast microtype and partially clipped navigation reduce polish. Contrast checks are incomplete at tablet/mobile, so full visual legibility is not proven.",
